  "live_records": {
    "q-77588": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77588",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/d828b48f347d79f8a6536ca178f5bb24bd46f6d35c278ca21bebdbb9a1b86750.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements best describes the triangle above?",
      "worked_solution": "In the above triangle, we see two congruent sides,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BC},\n$$\n\nbut the third side is not congruent:\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC}≇\\overset{―}{AC}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since only two sides are congruent, $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overset{―}{AC}.$\n\nOn the other hand, $∠B$ is a right angle. Therefore, $△ABC$ is a right isosceles triangle.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
