      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/171cff06ab08f9ce49acd6b203c074ec329abdc35caca357221329980c85f531.png)\n\nOrder the angles of the triangle $△ABC$ from smallest to largest.",
      "worked_solution": "The shortest side is $\\overset{―}{AC},$ so the smallest interior angle is $∠B.$\n\nThe longest side is $\\overset{―}{BC},$ which means that the opposite angle, $∠A$, must be the largest one.\n\nTherefore, the required order must be\n\n$$\n∠B,\\,∠C,\\,∠A.\n$$",
