      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/e7eb91b29c5a284d1ec7d487df5693dd5b10a18ff21dc1ef6223e47d32474e5b.png)\n\nOrder the angles of the triangle $△XYZ$ from smallest to largest.",
      "worked_solution": "The longest side is $\\overset{―}{XZ},$ which means that the opposite angle, $∠Y$, must be the largest one.\n\nThe shortest side is $\\overset{―}{YZ},$ so the smallest interior angle is $∠X.$\n\nTherefore, the required order must be\n\n$$\n∠X,\\,∠Z,\\,∠Y\\,.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
